---
import CtaBand from "../components/cta-band.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/page-header.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import Layout from "../layouts/index.astro";

const principles = [
	{
		title: "Learn against a known answer",
		detail:
			"Cloning a product everyone knows means you can always check your work, so the hard part is the engineering, not guessing what to build.",
	},
	{
		title: "Build as a team",
		detail:
			"Real software is handed between people. Every role depends on the others, and learning to hand work over well is half the job.",
	},
	{
		title: "Ship to production",
		detail:
			"Nothing counts until it's deployed, monitored and used by someone. Every team launches twice: the clone, then its own product.",
	},
	{
		title: "Founders first",
		detail:
			"We teach what a founder needs to build, hire and make good technical decisions, and skip what only matters in a job interview.",
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description={`Why ${site.founder} started Clonecademy, a bootcamp that teaches founders software engineering by cloning real products as a team.`}
>
	<PageHeader title="Founders shouldn't be locked out of their own product" />

	<section class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-7xl gap-14 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:px-8">
		<div class="lg:col-span-4">
			<!-- TODO: replace with a photo of the founder. -->
			<div
				class="bg-drafting relative grid aspect-4/5 max-w-xs place-items-center rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-ink"
				role="img"
				aria-label={`Photo of ${site.founder}`}
			>
				<span class="display text-7xl text-ink">KA</span>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-5 font-semibold">{site.founder}</p>
			<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Founder, {site.name}</p>
		</div>

		<!-- TODO: founder's note is draft copy. Rewrite in your own voice. -->
		<div class="typeset text-lg lg:col-span-7 lg:col-start-6">
			<p>
				I started Clonecademy after watching too many good founders lose
				their companies to their own codebase. They'd hired an agency or a
				freelancer, shipped something, and then couldn't change it, price
				it or even tell whether it was built well.
			</p>
			<p>
				Bootcamps weren't the answer. They're built to get people hired, so
				they teach one person to do everything, alone, on toy projects.
				Founders need the opposite: to understand how a whole product fits
				together, and how to work with the people who build each part.
			</p>
			<p>
				So every Clonecademy cohort is a team. Four founders, four roles, one
				real product that everyone already knows how to use. When you're
				stuck, you can open Amazon or Instagram and see how it should work.
				When you're done, you point the same team at one of your own ideas.
			</p>
			<p>
				You won't leave as a senior engineer in sixteen weeks. You'll leave
				able to build, read and make decisions about your own product, and
				that changes what kind of company you can build.
			</p>
			<p>Karthik</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="border-y border-border bg-muted/50">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-[-0.025em] sm:text-4xl">How we teach</h2>
			<dl class="mt-12 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
				{
					principles.map((item) => (
						<div>
							<dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{item.title}</dt>
							<dd class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{item.detail}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
		<p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			{site.name} is run by {site.company} Questions, partnerships and press:
			<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="font-medium text-foreground hover:text-primary">
				{site.email}
			</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<CtaBand />
</Layout>
